WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.680
A lot of us wish we could travel the multiverse,&nbsp;
pay a visit to another world and see all the ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.800
in which it differs from this dimension that we&nbsp;
call home. Maybe there’s a decision that you made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.080
that altered the course of your entire life –&nbsp;
what college you went to, asking somebody out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.120
accepting a job over pursuing a passion.&nbsp;
The question of ‘what if’ might have kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.600
you wondering what your life could have&nbsp;
looked like if you picked the other path.&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.760
Surely it would save you all that wondering and be&nbsp;
so much easier just to go and find out. Imagine if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.680
you could simply pick a universe where you chose&nbsp;
differently, then take a quick jaunt over there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.680
to see how things turned out for your other self.
But what if you couldn’t choose?&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.280
Never mind whatever that decision was; what if you&nbsp;
couldn’t pick where in the infinite multiverse you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.200
ended up? If traveling from world to world was&nbsp;
as random, unpredictable, and instinctive as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.800
a sneeze, what then? One moment you’re safe&nbsp;
at home, surrounded by everything you know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.840
It might not be perfect, but at least it's&nbsp;
familiar. The next thing you know, with a blink of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.880
your eyes, you’re standing in a world that maybe&nbsp;
looks similar, but giant bees are the dominant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.360
species instead of humans. Or the world is overrun&nbsp;
by spiders, or everyone is made out of paint.&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.880
Needless to say, you’d be at&nbsp;
least a little disorientated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:26.480
at worst absolutely terrified for your life.
That pretty much sums up the experience of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:33.760
SCP-507, also known as the Reluctant Dimension&nbsp;
Hopper. From the outside, he looks to be a mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.680
normal human man, with blonde hair, green eyes;&nbsp;
nothing all that remarkable about him of note&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:46.800
save for him having a somewhat unplaceable accent.&nbsp;
Despite having a legal name, SCP-507 will try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.280
squeeze what little enjoyment he can out of&nbsp;
introducing himself by a different nickname&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:58.000
to everyone he meets; previous favorites have&nbsp;
included Tommy, Steve, Bruto, Guy, Houdini,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.000
and Grabnok the Destroyer. We’ll stick with Tommy.
The sole most intriguing thing about Tommy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.600
is that, through a process that&nbsp;
happens completely without his control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:14.240
he can spontaneously disappear, only to reappear&nbsp;
after an unspecified amount of time later. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:21.040
that time, SCP-507 will have been in a completely&nbsp;
different universe to our own. This can happen at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.320
any time of day or night – and usually at&nbsp;
the most inconvenient moments; including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:33.200
while Tommy is in the middle of a conversation,&nbsp;
trying to sleep, or using the… ‘facilities.’&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.800
He had no control over when it happens, however,&nbsp;
he'll always arrive in an alternate universe in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:44.240
the same geographical spot he was in while in&nbsp;
ours. If he moves around in a parallel world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:50.240
then when he returns, he will have relocated to&nbsp;
the corresponding place back in this universe.&nbsp;

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.880
And that’s when disaster struck.
Alarms were blaring, declaring to all staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.520
on-site that there had been a containment breach&nbsp;
in one of the anomaly’s holding cells. All hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.280
were on deck, and security teams were converging,&nbsp;
dashing through the corridors. This was the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:12.240
alert today, at first SCP-507 had vanished on one&nbsp;
of his unplanned little excursions, but now it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:19.200
seemed that another SCP was trying to do the same.
Dazed, trying to reorientate himself, Tommy rested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:24.560
against a nearby wall. His head was spinning,&nbsp;
and he knew it would for a few more seconds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:30.320
He was in a cell, similar to the one he’d just&nbsp;
been in while in another universe. Except here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:36.480
back home, there was a key difference: The cell&nbsp;
was occupied. As soon as his vision cleared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.320
Tommy looked up at the only other creature&nbsp;
in the room with him. It was a tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:47.440
wiry humanoid shape, completely hairless with&nbsp;
pale skin, white eyes, and a large, gaping jaw.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.400
Turning to face him, Tommy instantly recognized&nbsp;
the creature from a description he’d been read by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:59.520
a Foundation researcher: it was SCP-096.
Uh oh, spaghetti-o’s.&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.040
Realizing its face was being observed, the Shy Guy&nbsp;
started screeching, first an uncontrollable wail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:10.640
of distress that quickly gave way to a guttural,&nbsp;
animalistic roar of anger. It covered its face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:16.320
babbling to itself as Tommy backed away, banging&nbsp;
his hand against the sealed wall of 096’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.520
cell. Then, the creature turned towards him,&nbsp;
and lunged, racing across the room to where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:28.240
SCP-507 was trapped. All he could do was close&nbsp;
his eyes tight and think about running away…&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.520
Tommy could feel a headache brewing in his skull,&nbsp;
and caught traces of a familiar flash through his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:39.120
closed eyelids. He gently opened them back up.&nbsp;
It had happened again, maybe for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.800
ever at a moment when he actually needed to get&nbsp;
away. Staggering to his feet, Tommy looked around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.560
He was in the cell still, or rather, another&nbsp;
version of it in a different universe yet again.&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.240
Knowing that he wouldn’t be able to&nbsp;
predict when he would next displace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.840
he didn’t want to reappear right back where he&nbsp;
had started, with SCP-096 poised to kill him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:05.360
So, relocating was top priority. Fortunately,&nbsp;
the cell actually had a door in this universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.720
and that door wasn’t locked. In fact, none&nbsp;
of the doors were locked or even guarded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.080
and the Foundation facility, while looking more&nbsp;
or less the same, was completely abandoned. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:21.200
almost looked like it had never even been used.
Stepping out of the entrance, Tommy trekked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:26.720
his way towards the city. He knew it was a short&nbsp;
hike away, and by the time he could feel blisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:32.000
forming on his feet, he was close enough that it&nbsp;
didn’t matter. Within another few short steps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.120
he was standing among the tall buildings and&nbsp;
surprisingly empty streets. One of the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.680
things that struck Tommy about this universe&nbsp;
was that there were hardly any people around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:48.000
outside. On top of that, the roads were devoid&nbsp;
of cars. Everything around was so quiet; the air&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.400
was still and clean when he breathed it in.
The sound of footsteps against the pavement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:57.680
immediately caught Tommy’s attention, the first&nbsp;
sign of anyone else around other than him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:02.320
Racing towards the noise of another person,&nbsp;
Tommy turned a corner and bumped straight into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:07.360
an old man in a long coat, who had clearly&nbsp;
been in a hurry, and quickly revealed he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.600
didn’t have the best temperament either.
“Watch where you’re going!” he shouted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.120
caught off-guard by the sight of another person&nbsp;
put on the streets. “What in the hell are you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.720
playing at, sneaking up on me like that?&nbsp;
You trying to get yourself killed out here?”&nbsp;

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:23.680
“Oh, definitely not!” Tommy said, climbing back&nbsp;
to his feet, hands held out apologetically.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.800
“I’m so sorry mister, I was just-”
“You got a death wish or something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:33.440
kid?” the old man demanded, marching past him.
“No!” SCP-507 protested, chasing after the man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.240
“Wait, what makes you say that?”
“As if you don’t know,” he scoffed. “Look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.040
around you, look up at the sky! There’s a storm&nbsp;
about to hit, any second now, it’s a-coming. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.160
if you don’t get inside, you’re a goner.”
“What could be so dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.240
about a thunderstorm?” Tommy asked.
The old man stared back at him with a look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:56.000
of confusion on his wizened face, looking at Tommy&nbsp;
like he had just said something utterly bizarre.&nbsp;

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:02.240
“What the hell’s a thunderstorm?” the man asked.
Feeling equally confused, Tommy craned his neck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:07.760
up towards the sky. Looming above were a swirling&nbsp;
mass of clouds, the kind anyone would expect to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:13.520
be accompanied by severe winds, and the deafening&nbsp;
boom of thunder. But the wind was still, and there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:20.160
was nothing but silence. Until a choking, gurgling&nbsp;
sound came from somewhere behind Tommy’s back.&nbsp;

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:26.880
He spun back around to see the tall, wiry frame of&nbsp;
SCP-096, its long fingers gripping tightly around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:32.640
the old man’s throat. It had followed Tommy, and&nbsp;
he knew that anyone who saw its face, even in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:37.760
picture, would find themselves chased down on foot&nbsp;
by the creature. But he had no idea the Shy Guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.800
could travel between dimensions. He’d foolishly&nbsp;
allowed himself to think that he was safe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:48.160
out of the monster’s reach, but now it seemed&nbsp;
to be showing him that the opposite was true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.800
It hoisted the helpless old man upwards by&nbsp;
his neck, his shoes barely able to graze the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:58.160
pavement as his legs flailed, eyes rolling&nbsp;
back as the Shy Guy clamped his throat shut.&nbsp;

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:03.280
The very second Tommy turned to run, the clouds&nbsp;
churned above and, without so much as a warning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:08.080
the storm hit. Something wasn’t right, Tommy&nbsp;
could feel his feet lifting off the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:13.840
immediately panicking as he thought SCP-096&nbsp;
had grabbed him. But, looking over his shoulder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.640
showed the creature was still a few feet&nbsp;
behind, and starting to gently float up off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:24.080
ground too. Instinctively, Tommy’s legs started&nbsp;
thrashing around, trying to gain a solid footing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:29.840
Instead, all his urgent motions did was cause him&nbsp;
to start spinning uncontrollably, as the gravity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:35.440
storm lifted him higher and higher into the air.
Spinning around as he was taken further upwards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:41.920
Tommy caught sight of SCP-096. The Shy Guy was&nbsp;
staying still, as if it was still in control of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:47.120
its body’s motion while he was wildly flipping&nbsp;
over himself. The tall, pale creature drifted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.680
closer to the side of a nearby building,&nbsp;
with Tommy barely able to reach the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.560
of the streetlights as he was pulled further&nbsp;
away from the safety of having both his feet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:02.560
on the ground. Just as he saw SCP-096 push itself&nbsp;
off the edge of the building, drifting straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.760
through the air towards him, Tommy shut his&nbsp;
eyes again and prayed he’d displace again.&nbsp;

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.680
Sure enough, a flash of light came&nbsp;
bursting out in time with another headache.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:16.080
Suddenly, he had appeared in the exact&nbsp;
same spot in another universe. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:21.440
here there was no gravity storm in progress&nbsp;
here. In fact, no such phenomena existed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:27.280
the laws of physics were much more in keeping with&nbsp;
those in Tommy’s home, our universe. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:33.360
that would be more reassuring if he wasn’t already&nbsp;
several feet up in the air. The second he arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.600
Tommy started plummeting back down to&nbsp;
Earth, screaming as he felt himself falling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:42.720
keeping his eyes screwed shut as he dared not look&nbsp;
at the ground he was currently hurtling towards.&nbsp;

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.920
His plummet was broken by something, not&nbsp;
particularly soft. Whatever it was seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:52.640
to tower high enough that Tommy only picked&nbsp;
up a few bruises as he hit it. But the fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:57.840
didn’t stop instantly, instead, he kept on&nbsp;
toppling through whatever he had landed on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:04.960
It was some kind of mass, piled up almost as tall&nbsp;
as a building, a collection of lots of… things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:09.280
that were all brushing past Tommy the more&nbsp;
he fell. He hadn’t yet stopped for long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:14.160
enough to recognize the sensations, that&nbsp;
is, until he landed with a painful thud.&nbsp;

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:19.040
Slowly opening his eyes back up, Tommy could&nbsp;
barely see anything in front of him. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:24.160
so deep in the mass that the pile was blocking&nbsp;
out the sunlight, with only a few beams bleeding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.480
through the gaps, but barely enough to&nbsp;
give him a clear view of where he was.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:33.440
Tommy tried to crawl forward, squeezed between&nbsp;
the heavy things around him, pushing though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:38.560
whatever tiny little crevice he could find. As he&nbsp;
did, the weight of the pile shifted around him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:43.200
and he was worried that any moment he would move&nbsp;
the wrong part of it, bringing the whole structure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:49.040
collapsing down on top of him like a toppled jenga&nbsp;
tower, only big enough to crush him to death.&nbsp;

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:54.000
He forced himself not to think about exactly what&nbsp;
the pile was made of either. It was already long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.000 --> 00:11:00.320
past the point where Tommy recognized what each…&nbsp;
thing felt like. Plus, there was the added stench,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:06.400
something – or lots of somethings – rotting and&nbsp;
producing a stomach-turning odor as it decayed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:11.360
Even when you’re trying not to look, it can be&nbsp;
hard to mistake the feeling of a hand, an arm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:16.160
cold skin against his. The light from&nbsp;
beyond the pyramid was getting closer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:20.160
he could see it was starting to illuminate more&nbsp;
of his surroundings the close her crawled to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:24.960
perimeter. Sure, he could have very easily used&nbsp;
the torch the Foundation let him keep with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:29.040
But Tommy wasn’t quite ready to see what&nbsp;
he was crawling through yet, intentionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.760
shutting his eyes and opting instead to follow&nbsp;
the faint glow and distant warmth of the sun.&nbsp;

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:39.680
Breaching the outer side of the pile, Tommy gulped&nbsp;
down lungfuls of air. It barely tasted or smelled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:45.040
that much cleaner than the air within the mass,&nbsp;
but at least he was free. Clawing himself out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:51.280
along the ground, he finally, carefully, stood up,&nbsp;
still keeping both eyes screwed shut. Part of him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:55.920
really didn’t want to take a look around this&nbsp;
new dimension, maybe if he waited long enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.920 --> 00:12:01.840
he would displace again and end up somewhere&nbsp;
with less… decomposing. But then he remembered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:08.640
SCP-096 was still after him, and he had no idea&nbsp;
how to escape it. He needed to try and figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:14.800
out what he was going to do, and the only way&nbsp;
to do that… was to look around at where he was.&nbsp;

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:20.320
Lifting his eyelids, the different sized masses&nbsp;
of all shades, shapes and sizes lay before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:26.080
him. Each one was coated in one unifying&nbsp;
color, all of them slick with the crimson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:30.960
of blood against skin. Tommy could feel the urge&nbsp;
to throw up quickly shooting up from the pit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:35.600
of his stomach towards his throat as he looked&nbsp;
at the massive pile of bodies in front of him.&nbsp;

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:40.960
It was enormous, there were so many dead people&nbsp;
all laying on top of one another that the pile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:45.520
reached up as tall as office buildings. And&nbsp;
the pile that he had fallen into and crawled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:52.240
his way out of wasn’t the only one either. As&nbsp;
far as the eye could see, everyone was dead.&nbsp;

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:57.040
Feeling a heavy sob at the back of his throat,&nbsp;
Tommy swallowed it when he heard another sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:03.520
above the low buzzing of flies over the human&nbsp;
carcasses. Someone… something else was crying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:09.280
nearby, and the moment he turned around,&nbsp;
the familiar figure caught Tommy’s eye. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:14.560
without being the only other living thing around&nbsp;
for miles, the Shy Guy still stood out clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:19.840
as day. Its distress at finding itself in this&nbsp;
horrible dimension briefly mirrored Tommy’s own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:25.760
until it restablished its psychic link&nbsp;
with its victim and gave chase once more.&nbsp;

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:31.840
SCP-096 started dashing towards SCP-507. For&nbsp;
a split second, he thought about just letting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:36.560
it catch him; what difference would it make in a&nbsp;
place like this? But then, the hallucinations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:42.720
bright colors and a stinging deep within his skull&nbsp;
hit Tommy. And just like that, he was gone again.&nbsp;

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:47.520
It was nighttime in the next dimension Tommy&nbsp;
arrived in. The cold air and dim light of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:52.160
street were enough to give that away. But at&nbsp;
least he was away from that last world filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:58.000
with discarded and unburied piles of corpses,&nbsp;
he thought to himself. Surely, he couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:02.720
possibly be anywhere worse than that now…
The first sight that Tommy was met with was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:09.120
a huge, white LCD screen, big enough to cover the&nbsp;
entire side of one of the skyscrapers facing him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.880
Emblazoned against the bright&nbsp;
white glow was a familiar symbol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:18.560
a circle with three arrows crossing its outline&nbsp;
and pointing towards its center. Around that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:24.800
a thin frame, another circle, this one with three&nbsp;
protruding rectangles around the circumference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:31.280
in line with the arrow tails. Thick lettered text&nbsp;
appeared on the screen too, beneath the emblem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:37.200
boldly proclaiming that anyone reading&nbsp;
it should ‘Submit. Comply. Persevere.’&nbsp;

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:41.520
Tommy blinked in disbelief, looking around.&nbsp;
There was hardly anyone else around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:46.560
save for a few people staring at him; had they&nbsp;
seen him appear? Or was it just because he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:50.880
dressed so differently to them? Each of&nbsp;
them had on a grimy pair of overalls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:56.240
sporting more of that same symbol on the chest&nbsp;
and across the back. Every wall of every nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.240 --> 00:15:01.120
building was overfilled with posters featuring&nbsp;
matching imagery, each one posing different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:06.800
questions in the same unforgiving, accusatory&nbsp;
text against its clinical white background.&nbsp;

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:12.320
One poster read ‘Could you be anomalous? Submit&nbsp;
for testing today.’ Another had the following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:19.440
notice: ‘Curfew still in effect, 10am to 8am the&nbsp;
following morning. All citizens must Comply.’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:24.640
And one more touted that ‘Only through&nbsp;
Persevering will we all continue to thrive.’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:29.520
Each of them was signed with the same name and&nbsp;
logo to match, the organization that Tommy had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:34.720
come to put some amount of trust in, even though&nbsp;
they weren’t always clear with him. But he knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:39.200
they weren’t the bad guys, or at least, the&nbsp;
version that existed in his universe didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:45.840
seem to be too bad. They had questionable&nbsp;
methods, but they weren’t evil… weren’t this.&nbsp;

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:51.200
“By order of the SCP Foundation!” A loud,&nbsp;
militaristic voice barked from behind Tommy. “Get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.600
down on your knees with your hands behind your&nbsp;
head. You will surrender any anomalous technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:59.920
and declare any memetic effects or cognito&nbsp;
hazardous abilities before we approach you.”&nbsp;

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:04.000
Tommy looked over his shoulder, met with the&nbsp;
barrels of several automatic weapons that were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:09.680
now being trained on him. Instantly he threw his&nbsp;
hands in the air, terrified that this alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:15.760
SCP Foundation might be far more trigger-happy&nbsp;
than the version of them he was used to. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:20.400
the look at the oppressive text on the huge&nbsp;
screen, the propaganda posters and the matching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:26.800
uniforms ordinary people seemed forced to wear,&nbsp;
this Foundation seemed to be far more ruthless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:31.040
They had transformed from a secretive&nbsp;
organization into a full-blown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:38.240
authoritarian regime, maybe even in control&nbsp;
of the entire world, ruling with an iron fist.&nbsp;

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:41.920
“On your knees!” the commander of&nbsp;
the Mobile Task Force shouted again.&nbsp;

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:45.200
The aggression in his voice, as well&nbsp;
as the several laser pointers from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:50.000
his men’s’ guns that were hovering over his&nbsp;
chest, prompted Tommy to do as he was told.&nbsp;

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:54.240
“Do you have anything to declare before&nbsp;
we approach?” the MTF leader barked.&nbsp;

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:59.520
“N-no!” Tommy stammered before realizing&nbsp;
that was probably an inadvisable answer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:05.840
“I mean, yes! I’m… I’m SCP-507, but that number&nbsp;
might refer to someone different here. Look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:09.520
what I’m saying is, this isn’t my dimension,&nbsp;
okay? I have a condition that sends me to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.160
different universes at random, I can’t&nbsp;
control it, it just happens. Please,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:15.200
for the love of god, don’t shoot!”
“Better radio into command,” the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:19.440
team leader told one of his subordinates. “Tell&nbsp;
them to run that number against the Archives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:23.360
then inform Lord Adjudicator Clef that&nbsp;
we may have a containment breach.”&nbsp;

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:27.600
Overhearing what they were saying instantly&nbsp;
reminded Tommy that he was still being chased.&nbsp;

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:31.360
“Wait,” he called to the elite operatives.&nbsp;
“There’s something else you need to know!”&nbsp;

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:35.200
“What’s that, 507?” the commander&nbsp;
sighed, lacking the patience for this.&nbsp;

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:39.840
“There’s another anomaly after me!” Tommy&nbsp;
explained hurriedly. “I don’t know how long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:44.000
it’ll take to get here, just that when it&nbsp;
does… it’ll kill everyone to get at me.”&nbsp;

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.440
“I’ve heard enough, troopers take&nbsp;
him away,” the commander grunted.&nbsp;

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:51.440
Two of the MTF team rushed up to Tommy and&nbsp;
grappled either of his arms, not letting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:56.400
go despite his protests. They started dragging&nbsp;
him towards their armored vehicle, looking like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.400 --> 00:18:00.240
Tommy was about to spend the foreseeable future&nbsp;
in the clutches of one of the worst versions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:06.320
of the Foundation. That is, until a tall, pale&nbsp;
creature stepped out from behind the transport.&nbsp;

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:11.280
The MTFs were instantly frenzied, and yells of&nbsp;
another anomalous contact were quickly drowned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:16.480
out by the noise of gunfire. All the while, the&nbsp;
Shy Guy was casually moving between the amassed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:22.080
troops, gripping their heads, twisting them all&nbsp;
the way around until a sickening crunch rang out.&nbsp;

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:27.280
Dropped back to the ground, SCP-507&nbsp;
started to feel another headache coming on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:32.960
knowing that any second he’d displace again&nbsp;
and end up in another alternate universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:38.640
And for the first time today, he was okay with&nbsp;
that. It was better for their chase to go on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:44.240
if it meant that him and the Shy Guy didn’t&nbsp;
have to spend another minute in this universe.&nbsp;

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:47.440
Now, if you want to see another of the&nbsp;
Foundation’s most infamous anomalies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:51.360
going toe to toe with an unlikely&nbsp;
adversary from across the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:57.840
then go and check out “DEADPOOL VS SCP-682”! Or,&nbsp;
ever wanted to know what would happen if a deadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:02.160
malicious mask was combined with one of the&nbsp;
most powerful reality benders ever encountered?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:08.560
Then watch “WHAT IF SCP-343&nbsp;
WORE SCP-035?” to find out!

